Lab Sheet 1 – MongoDB Solutions (Questions 1–20)
Below are the complete MongoDB Shell commands with realistic sample data and expected outputs.
Sample Data Used
// Students documents
{ rollNo: 101, name: "Alice Smith", department: "CSE", semester: 3, cgpa: 8.5 }
{ rollNo: 102, name: "Bob Johnson", department: "ECE", semester: 4, cgpa: 7.8 }
{ rollNo: 103, name: "Charlie Brown", department: "CSE", semester: 3, cgpa: 9.0 }
{ rollNo: 104, name: "Diana Prince", department: "ME", semester: 2, cgpa: 8.2 }
1. Create database StudentDB and verify
use StudentDB
db.getName()
Output:
switched to db StudentDB
StudentDB
2. Create collections Students, Faculty, and Courses
db.createCollection("Students")
db.createCollection("Faculty")
db.createCollection("Courses")
show collections
Output:
{ "ok" : 1 }
{ "ok" : 1 }
{ "ok" : 1 }
Courses
Faculty
Students
3. Insert a single document into Students
db.Students.insertOne({
  rollNo: 101,
  name: "Alice Smith",
  department: "CSE",
  semester: 3,
  cgpa: 8.5
})
Output:
{
  "acknowledged" : true,
  "insertedId" : ObjectId("...")
}
4. Insert multiple documents
db.Students.insertMany([
  { rollNo: 102, name: "Bob Johnson", department: "ECE", semester: 4, cgpa: 7.8 },
  { rollNo: 103, name: "Charlie Brown", department: "CSE", semester: 3, cgpa: 9.0 },
  { rollNo: 104, name: "Diana Prince", department: "ME", semester: 2, cgpa: 8.2 }
])
Output:
{
  "acknowledged" : true,
  "insertedIds" : {
    "0" : ObjectId("..."),
    "1" : ObjectId("..."),
    "2" : ObjectId("...")
  }
}
